      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material mislabeling the event",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'historical spacecraft explosion' because the meme relies on the viewer's recognition of the ironic or misleading juxtaposition created by the text. The user must interpret the text as a false label that contrasts with the visual of a successful rocket launch, which is the core of the meme's intent. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the projection is onto the textual material that creates the cognitive dissonance.",
